From 6798f1aafef41de0b365637c8a2dd5e6f312e67f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: well0nez <8986239+well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 00:16:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 22/27] allwinner: h713: a test bench BL31 says so at every
 boot

SUNXI_STANDBY_UNMEASURED=1 makes SYSTEM_SUSPEND take a crust whose build
word carries a deep-sleep step nobody has measured (PLL LDO, AVCC). Such
a BL31 differed from the standby one only in one mask in the
disassembly: not a string, not a boot line, so an image taken by mistake
would have shown up neither in a UART log nor in a gate over the build.

It now prints "PSCI: test bench BL31: system suspend takes unmeasured
deep-sleep steps too" as a NOTICE on every boot, and the string is in
that image and in no other, for a build gate to refuse.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 plat/allwinner/common/sunxi_pm.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/plat/allwinner/common/sunxi_pm.c b/plat/allwinner/common/sunxi_pm.c
index 2fb3ff71f..f5996fb34 100644
--- a/plat/allwinner/common/sunxi_pm.c
+++ b/plat/allwinner/common/sunxi_pm.c
@@ -297,6 +297,10 @@ int plat_setup_psci_ops(uintptr_t sec_entrypoint,
 	} else {
 #if SUNXI_SYSTEM_SUSPEND
 		INFO("PSCI: System suspend is offered while the ARISC firmware allows it\n");
+#if defined(SUNXI_STANDBY_UNMEASURED) && SUNXI_STANDBY_UNMEASURED
+		/* Every boot of a test bench image says so, not only its code. */
+		NOTICE("PSCI: test bench BL31: system suspend takes unmeasured deep-sleep steps too\n");
+#endif
 #else
 		INFO("PSCI: Suspend is unavailable\n");
 #endif
